  "note": "Each register carries the survivor's complete name-metadata entry, authored from the reviewed source, and one drift: `unit` changes the unit of a named KU row (CVID 131); `missing` stops delivering a named KU row (CVID 233); `new` delivers a second 2021 KU row (CVID 334) in an edition the entry covers; `partial` omits the 2021 KU row from `records`; `window` ends the authored KU window at 2020-12-31. Each entry goes stale at its own file; the survivor is the applied twin.",
  "fails_if": "`compile_delivery_metadata` loosens one of its checks: skipping the target and peer evaluation keeps `unit`; skipping the column-window equality keeps `window`; skipping the owner-set equality together with the evaluation keeps `new` and `partial`. `missing` is refused by all three, and with all three skipped a later representation guard fails the build",
